-- title:
--   Extensions of 𝔽ₚ-Hopf algebras with reduced Cartier dual
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ (so that $\mathbb{Z}/p$ is a field) and let $K$, $B$, $Q$ be commutative rings in one universe, each equipped with a Hopf algebra structure over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose comultiplication is cocommutative and which is finite as a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-module. Suppose given a bialgebra homomorphism $j : K \to B$ over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ that is injective as a function, and a bialgebra homomorphism $\pi : B \to Q$ over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ that is surjective as a function, such that the kernel of $\pi$, viewed as a ring homomorphism, coincides with the ideal of $B$ generated by the image under $j$ of the augmentation ideal of $K$, i.e. of the kernel of the counit algebra map $K \to \mathbb{Z}/p$; suppose moreover the rank relation $\dim_{\mathbb{Z}/p} B = \dim_{\mathbb{Z}/p} K \cdot \dim_{\mathbb{Z}/p} Q$ holds. Here [`CartierDual (ZMod p) A`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDual.html#L12) is the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-linear dual $\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathbb{Z}/p}(A, \mathbb{Z}/p)$ with its induced commutative ring structure. Assuming that the Cartier duals of $K$ and of $Q$ are reduced rings, the conclusion is that the Cartier dual of $B$ is a reduced ring.
--
--   In the language of finite commutative group schemes over $\mathbb{F}_p$, this is the statement that an extension of a group scheme of multiplicative type by another of multiplicative type is again of multiplicative type, the hypotheses on $j$, $\pi$, the augmentation ideal and the ranks encoding the exactness of the corresponding sequence of group schemes. It is used in the inductive treatment of towers arising from $p$-divisible groups, via [`PDivisibleGroup.Tower.forall_isReduced_cartierDual_of_isReduced_cartierDual_one_zmodp`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.Tower.forall_isReduced_cartierDual_of_isReduced_cartierDual_one_zmodp).
